# VRAM Stability & Render Reliability Walkthrough

We have successfully hardened the dubbing pipeline to survive the high-stress requirements of an 86-minute film render on limited VRAM hardware.

## Changes Made

### 1. Aggressive VRAM Purge Utility
I implemented a "Nuclear Option" in [cuda_utils.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/utils/cuda_utils.py) that goes beyond standard cache clearing. It triggers multiple garbage collection cycles and waits for the Windows drivers to fully release the memory handles from the previous GPU process.

### 2. The Render Verification Loop
Modified [lipsync_musetalk.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/stages/lipsync_musetalk.py) to include a "3-Strike" retry rule. 
- **The Problem**: Previously, if a render failed mid-way (corrupted frame), the engine would silently move to the next chunk without lipsync.
- **The Fix**: The engine now verifies the output file exists and is >1KB. If it fails, it triggers an aggressive VRAM purge and **retries the render** automatically.

### 3. VRAM Headroom Handshake
The pipeline now checks for at least 1.5GB of free VRAM before it even attempts to boot a new child process. This prevents "Dead on Arrival" renders caused by memory fragmentation.

